248
00:18:01,907 --> 00:18:05,363
But I didn't put Chucky
in front of the TV.

249
00:18:05,693 --> 00:18:07,577
Enough. Okay?

250
00:18:08,522 --> 00:18:10,785
Give me a kiss.

251
00:18:10,829 --> 00:18:13,527
Good night, baby,
and happy birthday.

252
00:18:13,571 --> 00:18:15,268
Good night,
Aunt Maggie.

253
00:18:28,499 --> 00:18:29,761
[DOOR CLOSING]

254
00:18:32,285 --> 00:18:36,445
I told you she'd be mad at you
if you watched the news.

255
00:19:00,444 --> 00:19:02,489
MAN ON TV: I missed you, my dear.

256
00:19:02,533 --> 00:19:05,449
I was afraid you weren't
going to show up.

257
00:19:05,492 --> 00:19:07,538
Too bad about the accident.

258
00:19:07,581 --> 00:19:10,628
WOMAN ON TV: Yes. Papa told us
they just found it.

259
00:19:10,671 --> 00:19:12,108
How did you know?

260
00:19:12,151 --> 00:19:13,500
MAN: I must have
heard it somewhere.

261
00:19:13,544 --> 00:19:15,459
WOMAN: I haven't seen you in so long, darling.

262
00:19:15,502 --> 00:19:17,374
I mean, couldn't we take
a little walk, or something?

263
00:19:17,387 --> 00:19:20,147
It looks as though you haven't
had a breath of fresh air in days.

264
00:19:20,159 --> 00:19:21,465
MAN: A walk?
WOMAN: Of course.

265
00:19:21,508 --> 00:19:23,162
The air outside will do you good.

266
00:19:23,206 --> 00:19:24,729
Besides, you'll work up an appetite.

267
00:19:24,772 --> 00:19:26,209
Please.

268
00:19:26,252 --> 00:19:27,688
MAN: But, Janice,
surely it's going to rain.

269
00:19:50,189 --> 00:19:51,367
[GASPS]

270
00:19:52,365 --> 00:19:53,788
Andy?

271
00:19:54,541 --> 00:19:56,195
MAN: Depends on whether
there's an indictment.

272
00:19:56,239 --> 00:19:58,197
WOMAN: Well, they don't always...

273
00:20:15,606 --> 00:20:16,824
[THUDDING]

274
00:20:30,664 --> 00:20:32,013
Andy, is that you?

275
00:20:38,281 --> 00:20:39,499
[THUNDER CRASHING]

276
00:21:34,902 --> 00:21:36,307
[BANGING]
[SCREAMS]

277
00:22:08,284 --> 00:22:09,372
How did that happen?

278
00:22:09,415 --> 00:22:10,963
[PHONE RINGS]

279
00:22:10,982 --> 00:22:12,636
Uh... Hello?

280
00:22:12,679 --> 00:22:14,768
Hi. How's it going?
How's Andy?

281
00:22:15,682 --> 00:22:16,988
MAGGIE: Karen?

282
00:22:17,031 --> 00:22:18,598
Yeah. Who else would it be?
Is something wrong?

283
00:22:19,773 --> 00:22:20,861
Uh...

284
00:22:20,905 --> 00:22:22,341
No.

285
00:22:22,385 --> 00:22:23,588
[CHUCKLING]

286
00:22:23,641 --> 00:22:25,518
Everything's fine.

287
00:22:27,172 --> 00:22:29,566
Are you sure?
You don't sound like everything's fine.

288
00:22:29,609 --> 00:22:34,005
No, I just had a bit of
the alone-at-night willies. You know?

289
00:22:34,048 --> 00:22:37,095
Now,
would you stop worrying

290
00:22:37,138 --> 00:22:39,622
and give Criswell
a kick in the pants for me?

291
00:22:39,646 --> 00:22:40,707
[LAUGHING]

292
00:22:40,751 --> 00:22:42,361
You got it.

293
00:22:42,405 --> 00:22:44,581
Hey, listen, Maggie.
Thank you for everything.

294
00:22:44,624 --> 00:22:46,104
You're a real pal.

295
00:22:46,539 --> 00:22:47,888
Oh, yeah?

296
00:22:47,932 --> 00:22:50,369
Yeah, yeah.
Give Andy a kiss for me, will you?

297
00:22:50,413 --> 00:22:51,979
See you soon. Bye.

298
00:23:05,079 --> 00:23:06,211
[CLINKING]

299
00:23:30,757 --> 00:23:33,369
What is wrong with me?

300
00:23:33,412 --> 00:23:35,196
I'm scaring myself
half to death.

301
00:23:37,173 --> 00:23:38,809
[SCREAMING]

302
00:24:05,879 --> 00:24:07,620
POLICEMAN 1: Step away
from this barricade.

303
00:24:07,664 --> 00:24:10,667
Come on, move it back.
There's nothing to see.

304
00:24:10,691 --> 00:24:12,625
POLICEMAN 2: Now, let's move
this police line back here.

305
00:24:12,669 --> 00:24:14,932
Go on home, folks, please.

306
00:24:14,975 --> 00:24:16,803
[INDISTINCT CHATTERING]

307
00:24:25,899 --> 00:24:27,771
DETECTIVE: She was
on the sixth floor.

308
00:24:39,260 --> 00:24:42,468
- Miss, what do you think you're doing?
- I live here.

309
00:24:48,922 --> 00:24:50,054
Andy?

310
00:24:51,708 --> 00:24:54,327
Oh, no. Andy?

311
00:24:55,538 --> 00:24:56,672
Andy?

312
00:24:57,583 --> 00:24:58,758
Andy!

313
00:24:58,802 --> 00:25:00,020
Mommy!

314
00:25:00,717 --> 00:25:02,414
Oh, thank God.

315
00:25:03,589 --> 00:25:05,504
Are you all right?

316
00:25:05,548 --> 00:25:08,202
Oh, I'm so glad.
I got so scared when I...

317
00:25:08,246 --> 00:25:10,857
What's wrong?
Where's Maggie?

318
00:25:10,901 --> 00:25:13,120
She had an accident.

319
00:25:13,164 --> 00:25:14,948
Accident?
What kind of an accident?

320
00:25:14,992 --> 00:25:18,212
Mrs. Barclay,
I'm Detective Mike Norris, Homicide.

321
00:25:18,256 --> 00:25:20,432
Could I talk to you
out in the hall?

322
00:25:20,476 --> 00:25:22,857
- Why? What's happened to Maggie?
- Please?

323
00:25:25,263 --> 00:25:26,917
I'll be right back.

324
00:25:35,316 --> 00:25:36,927
Look, Mrs. Barclay...

325
00:25:44,412 --> 00:25:46,284
What?

326
00:25:46,327 --> 00:25:47,933
Miss Peterson's dead,
Mrs. Barclay.

327
00:25:47,957 --> 00:25:49,012
What?

328
00:25:51,942 --> 00:25:53,104
How?

329
00:25:53,158 --> 00:25:55,336
She fell from
your kitchen window.

330
00:25:55,380 --> 00:25:56,773
Oh, no.

331
00:25:59,515 --> 00:26:00,907
You all right?

332
00:26:01,908 --> 00:26:03,780
Yes.All right.

333
00:26:03,823 --> 00:26:04,868
Come on.

334
00:26:09,568 --> 00:26:11,527
Oh, Maggie.

335
00:26:11,570 --> 00:26:12,876
Did you check
over here?

336
00:26:14,704 --> 00:26:16,575
[CRYING]

337
00:26:16,619 --> 00:26:17,794
Oh, Maggie.

338
00:26:22,799 --> 00:26:24,975
You got any idea
what these are?

339
00:26:30,110 --> 00:26:31,652
No.

340
00:26:31,845 --> 00:26:35,289
MIKE: They look like footprints, don't they?
Very small footprints.

341
00:26:36,421 --> 00:26:37,724
What are you implying?

342
00:26:38,728 --> 00:26:39,912
I don't know.

343
00:26:40,556 --> 00:26:42,366
What would Andy be doing
up on the counter, right?

344
00:26:42,419 --> 00:26:43,437
- What?
- Besides,

345
00:26:43,471 --> 00:26:46,823
I already checked his closet.
None of his shoes matched these prints.

346
00:26:46,866 --> 00:26:50,087
Mommy? Mommy?

347
00:26:50,130 --> 00:26:53,133
Chucky wanted to know
what was going on.

348
00:26:53,177 --> 00:26:54,395
Andy, I want you to
go to bed.

349
00:26:54,439 --> 00:26:55,832
The detective and I
are very busy.

350
00:26:55,875 --> 00:26:56,920
But, Mom...

351
00:26:56,963 --> 00:26:58,312
Right now, please.

352
00:27:00,488 --> 00:27:02,229
MIKE: Andy.

353
00:27:02,273 --> 00:27:04,057
What do you got
on your feet?

354
00:27:05,189 --> 00:27:07,757
Good Guy PJ sneakers.

355
00:27:07,800 --> 00:27:09,715
Wow. Come here.

356
00:27:12,675 --> 00:27:13,937
Can I see
the bottoms of them?

357
00:27:13,980 --> 00:27:15,481
Sure.

358
00:27:16,504 --> 00:27:19,809
Look at this. There's a gun.
Is that a cowboy hat?

359
00:27:19,843 --> 00:27:22,946
Andy, get into bed.
I'll be in in a minute to tuck you in.

360
00:27:22,989 --> 00:27:24,600
- But, Mom...
- Right now.

361
00:27:30,388 --> 00:27:32,520
Why are you treating
Andy like this?

362
00:27:32,564 --> 00:27:35,402
If he says he doesn't know how those
footprints got there, then he doesn't.

363
00:27:36,046 --> 00:27:38,268
Look, Mrs. Barclay,
somebody made those footprints.

364
00:27:38,291 --> 00:27:39,359
If not Andy, then who?

365
00:27:39,383 --> 00:27:41,225
I don't know,
and I don't care.

366
00:27:41,268 --> 00:27:43,012
All I know is that
I've just lost my best friend tonight

367
00:27:43,035 --> 00:27:44,141
to a horrible accident

368
00:27:44,184 --> 00:27:45,838
and I would like
some time alone with my son,

369
00:27:45,882 --> 00:27:47,797
who I'm sure is just as upset
about this as I am.

370
00:27:47,840 --> 00:27:50,013
Okay. Sorry. I'm sorry.

371
00:27:50,316 --> 00:27:53,759
I'll clear everybody
out of here right away. Okay?

372
00:27:53,803 --> 00:27:56,675
Hey, guys, you done?
Let's go. Chop-chop.

373
00:27:56,719 --> 00:27:58,938
Let's go, everybody.
Out of here.

374
00:27:58,982 --> 00:28:00,766
POLICEMAN 1: Let's clear this up
over here. Come on.

375
00:28:00,810 --> 00:28:02,072
POLICEMAN 2: Okay.

376
00:28:02,115 --> 00:28:03,464
POLICEMAN 3: Let's go, Sid.

377
00:28:09,296 --> 00:28:13,953
What do you think was so important
about my sneakers, Chucky?

378
00:28:15,041 --> 00:28:17,478
You don't know either,
do you?

379
00:28:38,412 --> 00:28:40,719
Well, let me know if you find out
anything about those footprints.

380
00:28:40,763 --> 00:28:42,503
Mommy, Mommy.

381
00:28:42,547 --> 00:28:45,071
Mommy, I know who was
on the kitchen counter. I know, I know.

382
00:28:45,115 --> 00:28:47,204
- Andy, I thought I...
- Who, Andy? Who?

383
00:28:47,247 --> 00:28:48,553
Chucky!

384
00:28:48,945 --> 00:28:50,323
Your doll?

385
00:28:51,687 --> 00:28:52,818
KAREN: Andy,
that's enough stories for tonight.

386
00:28:52,862 --> 00:28:55,778
Now, come on, back to bed.
Now I mean it.

387
00:28:55,821 --> 00:28:57,040
But, Mom...

388
00:29:01,435 --> 00:29:03,263
Good night, Detective.

389
00:29:06,658 --> 00:29:08,291
What?Are you gonna call me?

390
00:29:08,365 --> 00:29:09,748
You don't give up,
do you?

391
00:29:09,792 --> 00:29:11,820
I just...
I hate loose ends.

392
00:29:11,853 --> 00:29:14,884
And I hate people
who don't know when to stop.

393
00:29:14,927 --> 00:29:17,112
[WHISTLES]
Ouch.

394
00:29:17,147 --> 00:29:18,703
A spirited lady.

395
00:29:18,756 --> 00:29:20,063
No kidding.

396
00:29:20,106 --> 00:29:21,977
I want that autopsy report
on my desk

397
00:29:22,010 --> 00:29:23,327
- first thing tomorrow.
- Yeah.

398
00:29:23,370 --> 00:29:26,128
And anything you can
find out about Mrs. Barclay and her son.

399
00:29:26,172 --> 00:29:28,910
You got it. Anything else
I can do for you, sir?

400
00:29:28,924 --> 00:29:32,728
Oh, yeah. Here.
Get this to the lab.

401
00:29:32,771 --> 00:29:34,033
I found it in the corner
of the kitchen.

402
00:29:34,077 --> 00:29:35,285
What is this?

403
00:29:35,318 --> 00:29:36,732
Possible murder weapon.

404
00:29:36,775 --> 00:29:37,795
No.

405
00:29:38,864 --> 00:29:40,736
Come on.
You're kidding me.

406
00:29:42,694 --> 00:29:45,088
Hey, you are kidding me,
aren't you?

407
00:29:50,049 --> 00:29:52,878
ANDY: 'Cause she saw you
walking and talking?

408
00:30:05,717 --> 00:30:09,460
I guess there was
no hiding from her.

409
00:30:13,725 --> 00:30:15,683
Andy, who are you talking to?

410
00:30:15,727 --> 00:30:16,728
Chucky.

411
00:30:28,827 --> 00:30:30,307
Chucky, huh?

412
00:30:30,350 --> 00:30:32,570
Yeah, sure,
Chucky.

413
00:30:32,613 --> 00:30:34,702
He's sitting
right over there.

414
00:30:38,228 --> 00:30:41,144
Chucky's been
talking to you, too, hasn't he?

415
00:30:41,187 --> 00:30:42,493
What's he been saying?

416
00:30:42,536 --> 00:30:44,974
All kinds of things.

417
00:30:45,017 --> 00:30:48,629
His real name is
Charles Lee Ray,

418
00:30:48,673 --> 00:30:53,547
and he's been sent down
from heaven by Daddy to play with me.

419
00:30:58,378 --> 00:31:01,817
He has, has he?
Anything else?

420
00:31:01,860 --> 00:31:05,692
Yes. He said Aunt Maggie
was a real b****

421
00:31:05,725 --> 00:31:08,127
and got
what she deserved.

422
00:31:08,171 --> 00:31:12,044
Andy, how can you say
something so horrible?

423
00:31:12,088 --> 00:31:14,493
I didn't say it.
Chucky did.

424
00:31:14,537 --> 00:31:15,874
Andy, stop it.

425
00:31:15,918 --> 00:31:19,225
You know perfectly well
that you're making this up.

426
00:31:19,269 --> 00:31:22,623
But I'm not. Chucky's alive.
Really, he is.

427
00:31:22,646 --> 00:31:25,884
Andy, Chucky...
Chucky's a doll.

428
00:31:25,928 --> 00:31:28,080
He's made of plastic
and stuffing.

429
00:31:28,104 --> 00:31:29,888
Look at him. Look at him.

430
00:31:29,932 --> 00:31:31,842
Now, does he look like
anything else to you?

431
00:31:31,856 --> 00:31:33,506
Don't, you'll hurt him.

432
00:31:33,530 --> 00:31:36,025
Andy, look!

433
00:31:36,068 --> 00:31:38,984
Now you don't really
think that Chucky is alive, do you?

434
00:31:39,028 --> 00:31:40,808
But he is.

435
00:31:40,841 --> 00:31:44,381
Andy, stop it. Please.

436
00:31:44,424 --> 00:31:48,864
It's 'cause of Aunt Maggie
you're yelling at me, isn't it?

437
00:31:51,954 --> 00:31:55,261
Yes.
Yes, I guess it is.

438
00:31:55,783 --> 00:31:57,394
I'm sorry.

439
00:31:57,437 --> 00:32:00,179
I'll stop
making up stories.

440
00:32:05,619 --> 00:32:06,969
Thanks, champ.

441
00:32:08,927 --> 00:32:11,016
Do you wanna sleep
in with me tonight?

442
00:32:11,060 --> 00:32:13,236
No, it's all right.

443
00:32:13,279 --> 00:32:15,107
I've got Chucky.

444
00:32:19,024 --> 00:32:20,678
Come on, into bed.

445
00:32:26,118 --> 00:32:27,815
Good night, sweetheart.

446
00:32:30,122 --> 00:32:31,384
I love you.

447
00:32:37,434 --> 00:32:38,565
Good night.

448
00:32:48,184 --> 00:32:52,231
You're right, Chucky.
She didn't believe me.

449
00:32:59,325 --> 00:33:01,545
Hi.
I like to be hugged.

450
00:33:01,588 --> 00:33:05,505
Good. I'd love to
hug you, too.

451
00:33:15,037 --> 00:33:16,777
[SCHOOL BELL RINGING]

452
00:33:19,955 --> 00:33:21,913
Hey.

453
00:33:21,957 --> 00:33:24,263
You sure you're all right
about last night?

454
00:33:24,307 --> 00:33:26,186
No bad dreams
about Aunt Maggie?

455
00:33:27,310 --> 00:33:29,529
And Chucky's
only a doll, right?

456
00:33:31,749 --> 00:33:34,317
All right, off to school
with you, then. I love you tons.

457
00:34:49,957 --> 00:34:53,004
MAN ON PA: 43rd street.
Next stop, 47th.

458
00:35:22,903 --> 00:35:24,775
[INDISTINCT CHATTERING]

459
00:35:45,361 --> 00:35:46,927
Is that Eddie's?

460
00:35:51,193 --> 00:35:55,586
Look, you stay here.
I have to go tinkle.

461
00:36:06,643 --> 00:36:09,185
I'll be right there, Chucky.

462
00:36:11,561 --> 00:36:12,953
[CHUCKY PANTING]

463
00:36:57,259 --> 00:36:58,434
[THUDDING]

464
00:37:12,187 --> 00:37:13,449
[GAS HISSING]

465
00:37:23,720 --> 00:37:25,432
Chucky?

466
00:37:26,026 --> 00:37:27,661
Chucky?

467
00:37:35,471 --> 00:37:36,950
[GUN COCKING]

468
00:38:07,981 --> 00:38:09,412
[CLANGING]

469
00:38:10,636 --> 00:38:11,637
[GASPS]

470
00:38:19,645 --> 00:38:20,951
Chucky?

471
00:38:27,305 --> 00:38:28,763
Chucky?

472
00:38:29,481 --> 00:38:30,787
Chucky?

473
00:38:31,918 --> 00:38:33,180
Chucky?

474
00:38:34,965 --> 00:38:36,009
[CRASHING]

475
00:38:43,669 --> 00:38:45,105
[GAS HISSING]

476
00:38:47,151 --> 00:38:48,195
Chucky?

477
00:38:52,504 --> 00:38:54,027
Chucky?

478
00:39:17,790 --> 00:39:19,207
Mrs. Barclay.

479
00:39:19,221 --> 00:39:22,030
Detective Norris,
I came as soon as I got your message.

480
00:39:22,104 --> 00:39:23,840
You haven't been
to the school to pick up your son yet?

481
00:39:23,883 --> 00:39:26,674
No. No, I came directly from work.
Why?

482
00:39:26,738 --> 00:39:27,963
Let's go into my office.

483
00:39:29,324 --> 00:39:30,499
Is something wrong
with Andy?

484
00:39:30,542 --> 00:39:31,543
Please.

485
00:39:34,503 --> 00:39:35,650
I...

486
00:39:39,943 --> 00:39:41,858
I don't know
how to tell you this, Mrs. Barclay.

487
00:39:41,901 --> 00:39:43,343
Tell me what?

488
00:39:43,556 --> 00:39:46,863
Do you have any idea why
your Aunt Maggie fell out of that window?

489
00:39:46,906 --> 00:39:47,951
Yes.

490
00:39:47,994 --> 00:39:49,920
Could you tell me why?

491
00:39:50,823 --> 00:39:55,741
'Cause she saw Chucky,
and it scared her so much, she fell out.

492
00:39:55,785 --> 00:39:57,090
Oh, she did, huh?

493
00:39:57,656 --> 00:40:00,629
[DOOR OPENING]
So why did Chucky go to see Eddie Caputo?

494
00:40:00,703 --> 00:40:02,095
Mommy!

495
00:40:02,139 --> 00:40:03,662
Oh, Andy.

496
00:40:07,840 --> 00:40:09,973
All right, sweetheart.
Come on.

497
00:40:12,323 --> 00:40:14,194
Now listen
to me, okay?

498
00:40:15,457 --> 00:40:19,025
Nobody believes you
about Chucky.

499
00:40:19,069 --> 00:40:22,250
Unless you start
telling the truth right now,

500
00:40:23,290 --> 00:40:25,902
they're going to
take you away from me.

501
00:40:28,644 --> 00:40:30,527
You hear that, Chucky?

502
00:40:30,531 --> 00:40:33,213
They're taking me away
unless you say something.

503
00:40:36,173 --> 00:40:38,044
Please, say something.

504
00:40:39,785 --> 00:40:42,527
Come on, Chucky.
Say something.

505
00:40:42,571 --> 00:40:46,052
Tell me why you lied to me
about everything.

506
00:40:46,096 --> 00:40:49,412
Come on, Chucky.
Say something.

507
00:40:49,534 --> 00:40:51,580
Tell me.

508
00:40:51,623 --> 00:40:56,085
Hi, I'm Chucky, and I'm your friend
to the end. Hidey-ho.

509
00:40:56,098 --> 00:40:57,107
[CHUCKY LAUGHS]

510
00:40:57,150 --> 00:40:58,369
[GRUNTS]

511
00:40:58,413 --> 00:41:01,459
Mommy, he's doing it
on purpose.

512
00:41:01,503 --> 00:41:05,768
He told me never to
tell about him or he'd kill me.

513
00:41:05,811 --> 00:41:09,641
Mrs. Barclay, my name is Dr. Ardmore.
I'm from County General.

514
00:41:09,685 --> 00:41:12,165
I've seen more than enough.

515
00:41:12,209 --> 00:41:15,168
Maybe Andy should spend
a couple of days with us.

516
00:41:52,771 --> 00:41:57,036
Well, say something,
you little bastard.

517
00:41:58,908 --> 00:42:01,259
Say something, damn it!

518
00:42:02,041 --> 00:42:04,261
Hi. I like to be hugged.

519
00:42:05,958 --> 00:42:07,394
[LAUGHING]

520
00:42:45,886 --> 00:42:47,634
"He wants you
for a best friend."

521
00:42:48,827 --> 00:42:50,089
Yeah, sure.

522
00:43:49,496 --> 00:43:52,751
- Hi, I'm Chucky. Wanna play?
- [SCREAMS]

523
00:44:55,084 --> 00:44:56,563
Talk to me.

524
00:44:58,087 --> 00:44:59,523
Come on, talk.

525
00:45:01,525 --> 00:45:04,145
I said, talk to me,
damn it. All right.

526
00:45:04,169 --> 00:45:06,617
Then I'm gonna
make you talk!

527
00:45:19,761 --> 00:45:23,503
I said talk to me, damn it,
or else I am gonna throw you in the fire!

528
00:45:23,547 --> 00:45:26,202
You stupid b****!
You filthy slut!

529
00:45:26,245 --> 00:45:28,855
I'll teach you to fuck with me!
No! No!

530
00:45:28,900 --> 00:45:30,815
[SCREAMING]

531
00:45:30,859 --> 00:45:32,382
[CHUCKY GRUNTING]

532
00:45:34,863 --> 00:45:36,516
[GROANS]

533
00:45:39,650 --> 00:45:40,695
[SCREAMING]

534
00:45:41,739 --> 00:45:42,740
[SCREAMING]

535
00:45:49,355 --> 00:45:50,443
[EXCLAIMS]

536
00:45:53,403 --> 00:45:54,621
[DOOR OPENING]

537
00:46:07,809 --> 00:46:08,999
Stop!

538
00:46:42,844 --> 00:46:44,311
No.

539
00:46:46,499 --> 00:46:47,500
No.

540
00:46:49,154 --> 00:46:50,503
[SOBBING]

541
00:46:51,026 --> 00:46:52,443
No!

542
00:47:02,080 --> 00:47:03,995
Detective Norris!

543
00:47:04,039 --> 00:47:05,954
Mrs. Barclay,
what are you doing back here?

544
00:47:05,997 --> 00:47:09,740
Andy was telling the truth.
Chucky is alive and he killed Eddie Caputo.

545
00:47:09,784 --> 00:47:10,828
What?

546
00:47:10,872 --> 00:47:12,104
I took him home
to my apartment.

547
00:47:12,137 --> 00:47:15,353
I was about to throw away the box that he
came in when the batteries fell out.

548
00:47:15,877 --> 00:47:17,214
Don't you see?

549
00:47:17,257 --> 00:47:20,272
He's been moving and talking for days
without any batteries in him.

550
00:47:20,316 --> 00:47:21,771
What are you talking about?

551
00:47:21,794 --> 00:47:23,667
How I found out
the doll was alive.

552
00:47:23,710 --> 00:47:25,930
See, I threatened
to throw him into the fireplace,

553
00:47:25,974 --> 00:47:28,803
when all of a sudden,
he came alive in my hand.

554
00:47:28,846 --> 00:47:31,718
I dropped him, and he got up and
ran out of the apartment.

555
00:47:32,415 --> 00:47:34,330
Good night, Mrs. Barclay.

556
00:47:34,373 --> 00:47:37,550
Wait a minute.
I am telling you the truth.

557
00:47:37,594 --> 00:47:39,221
He killed Maggie.
He killed Eddie Caputo.

558
00:47:39,254 --> 00:47:40,597
Look, Mrs. Barclay.

559
00:47:40,640 --> 00:47:42,773
I sympathize with you.
I really do.

560
00:47:42,817 --> 00:47:44,644
I hated what happened
in there today.

561
00:47:44,688 --> 00:47:46,376
But lying is not gonna
help your son.

562
00:47:46,399 --> 00:47:48,784
Lying? Does this look
like I'm lying?

563
00:47:50,389 --> 00:47:51,447
How did you get those?

564
00:47:51,500 --> 00:47:52,522
Chucky bit me.

565
00:47:52,565 --> 00:47:55,568
Oh, for God's sake.

566
00:47:55,612 --> 00:47:57,570
All right,
don't believe me.

567
00:47:59,137 --> 00:48:00,178
Where you going?

568
00:48:00,191 --> 00:48:01,531
To find Chucky.

569
00:48:01,574 --> 00:48:03,032
How you gonna do that?

570
00:48:03,106 --> 00:48:05,404
I bought him from a peddler
where I work. I'll start there.

571
00:48:05,448 --> 00:48:08,014
That isn't a good part of town to be
in at this time of night.

572
00:48:08,077 --> 00:48:10,105
Mrs. Barclay,
do you hear me?

573
00:48:10,148 --> 00:48:13,223
You don't want to
go down there at this time of night.

574
00:48:17,373 --> 00:48:19,157
God damn it.

575
00:48:48,143 --> 00:48:49,405
[INAUDIBLE]

576
00:49:18,129 --> 00:49:19,203
Uh-huh.

577
00:49:34,189 --> 00:49:35,799
What's she doing here?

578
00:49:40,195 --> 00:49:42,110
Hey, excuse me.

579
00:49:42,153 --> 00:49:43,415
Mister.

580
00:49:46,114 --> 00:49:47,854
Mister.

581
00:49:47,898 --> 00:49:50,205
I'm not gonna hurt you.
Do you remember me?

582
00:49:50,248 --> 00:49:51,384
No, no.

583
00:49:51,407 --> 00:49:52,878
I'm sorry.
I bought a doll from you

584
00:49:52,901 --> 00:49:55,159
in back of Carson's department store
with my friend yesterday.

585
00:49:55,192 --> 00:49:56,907
- Doll?
- Yes, a Good Guy doll.

586
00:49:56,951 --> 00:49:58,938
You sold it to me.
Do you remember?

587
00:49:58,972 --> 00:50:00,789
Oh, yeah, a doll.
What about it?

588
00:50:00,823 --> 00:50:02,391
Where did you get it?

589
00:50:02,434 --> 00:50:04,654
What will you give me
if I tell you?

590
00:50:04,697 --> 00:50:09,677
I don't have much, but you're
welcome to whatever I have.

591
00:50:12,053 --> 00:50:14,403
It's not enough.
What else you got?

592
00:50:15,317 --> 00:50:16,622
That's all I've got.

593
00:50:16,666 --> 00:50:18,189
All you got?

594
00:50:18,233 --> 00:50:20,401
- What are you... Yes.
- That's not all you got.

595
00:50:21,236 --> 00:50:23,008
- Wait a minute.
- No, you got a lot.

596
00:50:23,012 --> 00:50:24,935
No. No, no.

597
00:50:24,979 --> 00:50:28,112
[SCREAMING]
No. Wait. No, no!

598
00:50:28,156 --> 00:50:29,323
Pig!

599
00:50:30,027 --> 00:50:31,382
Christ, he's a cop!

600
00:50:31,425 --> 00:50:33,378
All right. What about
the rest of you?

601
00:50:33,422 --> 00:50:34,901
You wanna party, too?

602
00:50:41,778 --> 00:50:44,128
All right. Now, you want to answer
the lady's question now?

603
00:50:44,172 --> 00:50:46,210
Where did you get
the doll from?

604
00:50:46,224 --> 00:50:48,089
I don't know nothing
about no doll.

605
00:50:48,112 --> 00:50:50,016
You're not gonna know nothing
about nothing in a minute,

606
00:50:50,060 --> 00:50:51,496
unless you talk to me.
Now talk!

607
00:50:51,530 --> 00:50:54,704
A burned-out toy store on Wabash.
That's where I got it.

608
00:50:56,967 --> 00:50:58,360
Get out of here.

609
00:51:00,449 --> 00:51:01,841
What's wrong?

610
00:51:03,365 --> 00:51:04,409
Nothing.

611
00:51:06,585 --> 00:51:09,446
Well, wait a minute. Something the peddler
said upset you. What was it?

612
00:51:09,460 --> 00:51:12,243
I just told you,
nothing.

613
00:51:12,287 --> 00:51:15,881
God damn it.
My son's life is at stake. Now, what was it?

614
00:51:17,074 --> 00:51:20,817
The place where he said
he got the doll, Charles Lee Ray died there.

615
00:51:20,860 --> 00:51:22,102
Who?

616
00:51:22,155 --> 00:51:26,040
The Lake Shore Strangler.
The man who's partners with Eddie Caputo.

617
00:51:27,188 --> 00:51:28,684
Hey. Where are
you going now?

618
00:51:28,727 --> 00:51:29,981
Wabash and Van Buren.

619
00:51:29,994 --> 00:51:32,350
There's nothing there.
It's an abandoned wreck of a store.

620
00:51:32,394 --> 00:51:33,554
Why don't you believe me?

621
00:51:33,568 --> 00:51:36,659
It was struck by lightning
the night that Charles Lee Ray died.

622
00:51:38,704 --> 00:51:40,128
How do you know that?

623
00:51:40,182 --> 00:51:43,106
Because I was there.
I was the man who killed him.

624
00:51:49,802 --> 00:51:52,762
Why didn't you tell me?

625
00:51:52,805 --> 00:51:56,505
It's not exactly the kind of thing
you tell someone.

626
00:51:56,548 --> 00:51:59,986
Come on, let me take you home.
You need some sleep.

627
00:52:00,030 --> 00:52:01,857
Did he say anything?
Anything at all?

628
00:52:01,891 --> 00:52:03,207
- Who?
- Charles Lee Ray.

629
00:52:03,251 --> 00:52:06,142
Yeah. He threatened to kill me
and Eddie Caputo.

630
00:52:19,702 --> 00:52:22,444
I'm sorry you couldn't
find anything to help Andy.

631
00:52:22,487 --> 00:52:24,272
I really am.

632
00:52:24,315 --> 00:52:28,363
But I did. I found out that Chucky
is Charles Lee Ray.

633
00:52:28,406 --> 00:52:30,974
The only thing I don't know is how
he got inside the doll.

634
00:52:32,932 --> 00:52:34,294
Good night,
Mrs. Barclay.

635
00:52:34,318 --> 00:52:35,719
Where did
Charles Lee Ray live?

636
00:52:36,893 --> 00:52:39,156
Look, please, will you just
get out of the car?

637
00:52:39,200 --> 00:52:41,245
Hey, just tell me
where he lived.

638
00:52:41,289 --> 00:52:44,422
Don't you understand?
Andy's life depends on it.

639
00:52:44,466 --> 00:52:47,327
730 Stoney Island,
the south side.

640
00:52:47,351 --> 00:52:48,891
But I've already
checked the place out.

641
00:52:48,924 --> 00:52:51,212
There's nothing there.
Now, good night.

642
00:52:51,255 --> 00:52:52,814
Wait a minute.
Where are you going?

643
00:52:54,128 --> 00:52:56,260
- Home, to get some sleep.
- No, you can't do that.

644
00:52:56,304 --> 00:52:59,002
Don't you see?
You just said it.

645
00:52:59,045 --> 00:53:01,309
Chucky killed Caputo.
That leaves you.

646
00:53:01,352 --> 00:53:02,440
That does it.

647
00:53:02,484 --> 00:53:03,789
Oh, please
listen to me.

648
00:53:08,142 --> 00:53:09,186
Out.

649
00:53:09,230 --> 00:53:10,796
I am telling you
the truth.

650
00:53:10,840 --> 00:53:12,189
Why won't
you believe me?

651
00:53:12,233 --> 00:53:15,053
Because I'm sane, Mrs. Barclay.
Sane and rational.

652
00:53:16,889 --> 00:53:18,761
All right. All right.

653
00:53:18,804 --> 00:53:19,994
Do you remember
what you said

654
00:53:19,998 --> 00:53:21,507
the first night
you met me in my apartment?

655
00:53:21,550 --> 00:53:23,327
- What about it?
- You said you didn't like loose ends.

656
00:53:23,380 --> 00:53:24,541
Well, I'm a loose end.

657
00:53:24,574 --> 00:53:27,371
You can't just let go what I said tonight
without checking it out.

658
00:53:27,384 --> 00:53:29,511
For the last time,
Mrs. Barclay, good night.

659
00:53:29,554 --> 00:53:30,990
[GRUNTS IN ANNOYANCE]

660
00:54:02,370 --> 00:54:03,849
[STARTS ENGINE]

661
00:54:03,893 --> 00:54:05,329
[MUSIC PLAYING ON RADIO]

662
00:54:05,373 --> 00:54:07,833
♪ I go outside

663
00:54:10,552 --> 00:54:12,858
♪ Don't you lift the top

664
00:54:12,902 --> 00:54:15,165
♪ When you want to see inside

665
00:54:18,429 --> 00:54:21,215
♪ You can only see one thing

666
00:54:21,258 --> 00:54:24,245
♪ At a time
and that won't... ♪

667
00:54:24,305 --> 00:54:25,393
[SCREAMS]

668
00:54:27,786 --> 00:54:29,223
Good night, asshole.

669
00:54:37,579 --> 00:54:39,363
[LAUGHING]

670
00:54:51,288 --> 00:54:52,376
[SCREAMING]

671
00:55:00,341 --> 00:55:01,907
[CHOKING]

672
00:55:03,082 --> 00:55:04,083
[SCREAMS]

673
00:55:16,270 --> 00:55:17,687
[SCREAMS]

674
00:55:25,975 --> 00:55:27,498
MAN: Jeez, look out!

675
00:55:59,574 --> 00:56:01,053
[SCREAMING]

676
00:56:18,070 --> 00:56:19,615
Hi, Mikey.

677
00:56:20,536 --> 00:56:22,393
[GROWLING]

678
00:56:27,341 --> 00:56:28,603
[CHUCKY LAUGHS]

679
00:56:28,646 --> 00:56:32,035
Won't do you any good, Mikey.
You can't hurt me.

680
00:56:35,479 --> 00:56:36,654
[GUN FIRES]

681
00:56:42,486 --> 00:56:43,966
[CHUCKY LAUGHING]

682
00:56:47,709 --> 00:56:49,145
[GRUNTING]

683
00:57:14,083 --> 00:57:15,780
[SCREAMING]

684
00:57:15,824 --> 00:57:16,825
[GUN FIRES]

685
00:57:21,177 --> 00:57:22,178
[GUN FIRES]

686
00:58:10,139 --> 00:58:11,401
[SIGHS]

687
00:58:54,052 --> 00:58:55,489
[SCREAMS]
Karen.

688
00:58:57,665 --> 00:58:58,666
[EXHALES]

689
00:58:59,971 --> 00:59:01,930
What are you doing here?

690
00:59:03,627 --> 00:59:05,542
After I talked to you
last night,

691
00:59:05,586 --> 00:59:09,372
I decided to go back
to the station and pull Ray's file.

692
00:59:09,415 --> 00:59:12,506
I learned a couple of things.
His nickname was Chucky,

693
00:59:14,377 --> 00:59:16,858
and he spent a lot of time
with this man.

694
00:59:23,212 --> 00:59:26,128
Now, all we have to do is find him
before Chucky does.

695
00:59:34,963 --> 00:59:36,442
CHUCKY: Hello, John.

696
00:59:38,619 --> 00:59:39,837
Over here.

697
00:59:40,882 --> 00:59:42,583
Hi.

698
00:59:42,840 --> 00:59:44,799
It's me. Chucky.

699
00:59:44,842 --> 00:59:48,324
What do you think?
The grigri work?

700
00:59:50,413 --> 00:59:54,591
You know, when I came here learning
all that stuff about how to beat death,

701
00:59:54,635 --> 00:59:56,941
I thought maybe you were
pulling my chain.

702
00:59:56,985 --> 01:00:00,081
But not now. Not now.

703
01:00:00,466 --> 01:00:02,115
Only one problem.

704
01:00:02,169 --> 01:00:03,342
What?

705
01:00:04,166 --> 01:00:07,386
This. I didn't think
anybody could hurt me.

706
01:00:07,430 --> 01:00:09,183
But last night, I got shot.

707
01:00:10,085 --> 01:00:12,609
You know something?
It hurt.

708
01:00:12,653 --> 01:00:15,786
It hurt like a son of a b****.
It even bled.

709
01:00:15,830 --> 01:00:17,353
Now why's that, John?

710
01:00:18,049 --> 01:00:19,739
You're turning human.

711
01:00:19,753 --> 01:00:21,575
What?

712
01:00:21,618 --> 01:00:24,142
The more time
you spend in that body,

713
01:00:25,535 --> 01:00:29,234
the more human
you'll become.

714
01:00:29,278 --> 01:00:33,021
You mean I have to
live out the rest of my life in this body?

715
01:00:33,064 --> 01:00:36,546
No fucking way. You got me into this,
you get me out.

716
01:00:38,156 --> 01:00:39,854
I can't do that, Chucky.

717
01:00:39,897 --> 01:00:41,638
Why not?

718
01:00:41,682 --> 01:00:44,601
Because you're
an abomination,

719
01:00:45,294 --> 01:00:48,297
an outrage against nature.

720
01:00:48,340 --> 01:00:52,475
You perverted everything
I've taught you and used it for evil.

721
01:00:52,518 --> 01:00:54,259
And you have to be stopped.

722
01:00:58,307 --> 01:01:01,223
You know, I thought
something like this might happen.

723
01:01:01,266 --> 01:01:02,990
That's why
I prepared for it.

724
01:01:03,043 --> 01:01:04,966
What are
you talking about?

725
01:01:05,009 --> 01:01:06,924
Your own personal mojo, doc.

726
01:01:08,404 --> 01:01:09,666
Give me that.

727
01:01:09,710 --> 01:01:11,875
Sure.
How do you want it? Broken leg?

728
01:01:12,408 --> 01:01:15,411
[SCREAMS]

729
01:01:15,454 --> 01:01:19,458
Shouldn't tell your customers
where you hide things like this, John.

730
01:01:19,502 --> 01:01:22,026
Gets you in trouble
every time.

731
01:01:22,070 --> 01:01:24,550
Now how do I get out
of this body?

732
01:01:24,594 --> 01:01:26,746
No, I won't tell you.

733
01:01:26,810 --> 01:01:27,828
Yeah?

734
01:01:27,891 --> 01:01:30,208
[SCREAMS]

735
01:01:30,252 --> 01:01:33,864
Tell me or die, John.
Your choice.

736
01:01:33,908 --> 01:01:36,486
No, I'll tell you.

737
01:01:38,695 --> 01:01:42,133
You have to transfer your soul
out of the doll

738
01:01:42,177 --> 01:01:46,529
into that of the first
human being you revealed your true self to.

739
01:01:46,572 --> 01:01:50,142
You mean the first person
I let in on the fact that I was really alive?

740
01:01:51,099 --> 01:01:53,188
[LAUGHING]

741
01:01:53,231 --> 01:01:56,452
I don't believe it.
I just don't believe it.

742
01:01:56,495 --> 01:02:00,499
The first person I let in on my little secret
was a six-year-old kid.

743
01:02:00,543 --> 01:02:03,067
I'm gonna be
six years old again.

744
01:02:03,111 --> 01:02:07,332
Well, John, it's been fun,
but I gotta go.

745
01:02:07,376 --> 01:02:09,683
I have a date
with a six-year-old boy.

746
01:02:11,075 --> 01:02:14,180
And you have a date
with death.

747
01:02:15,689 --> 01:02:16,907
[GROANING]

748
01:02:17,516 --> 01:02:19,697
So long, John.

749
01:02:23,697 --> 01:02:25,307
[SIREN BLARING]

750
01:02:44,369 --> 01:02:46,284
Hold it. Wait, wait.

751
01:02:53,988 --> 01:02:55,511
Oh, my God.

752
01:02:57,556 --> 01:02:59,080
[DIALING]

753
01:02:59,123 --> 01:03:00,646
Too late.What?

754
01:03:01,735 --> 01:03:04,384
Must save the boy. Must...

755
01:03:07,088 --> 01:03:08,611
Must get his soul

756
01:03:09,873 --> 01:03:12,828
into him
like he got into doll.

757
01:03:12,876 --> 01:03:14,791
What?

758
01:03:14,835 --> 01:03:18,882
You must stop him
before he can say the chant.

759
01:03:18,926 --> 01:03:21,972
Kill him
before he can say it.

760
01:03:22,016 --> 01:03:24,496
But how? How?

761
01:03:24,540 --> 01:03:28,827
The heart.
His heart is almost human.

762
01:03:31,068 --> 01:03:34,858
It's the only way.
Through the heart.

763
01:03:41,383 --> 01:03:43,080
[CLANGING]

764
01:03:52,263 --> 01:03:56,799
Help me! Help me!
Dr. Ardmore, Chucky's here!

765
01:04:06,234 --> 01:04:10,889
Help me! He's coming to kill me!
He's here. Chucky's here.

766
01:04:10,933 --> 01:04:12,981
I don't see anybody.

767
01:04:14,242 --> 01:04:16,679
But, Doctor,
Chucky's here,

768
01:04:16,722 --> 01:04:18,681
and he's going to kill me.

769
01:04:22,250 --> 01:04:27,300
But Chucky is here,
and he's going to kill me!

770
01:04:29,866 --> 01:04:32,477
He's going to kill me.

771
01:04:32,521 --> 01:04:35,840
Please don't leave me.
Please.

772
01:04:36,481 --> 01:04:38,048
[CRYING]

773
01:04:43,619 --> 01:04:45,490
[IS IT REALLY LOVE
PLAYING ON RADIO]

774
01:05:24,878 --> 01:05:26,101
[GASPS]

775
01:05:28,316 --> 01:05:29,404
No!

776
01:05:32,276 --> 01:05:33,756
ARDMORE: Andy, stop.

777
01:05:33,799 --> 01:05:35,556
ATTENDANT: Hey, wait a minute.

778
01:05:35,599 --> 01:05:36,672
Stop him!

779
01:05:49,728 --> 01:05:50,904
MAN: Check the north corridor.

780
01:05:59,477 --> 01:06:00,739
[SCREAMING]

781
01:06:35,383 --> 01:06:37,211
[ANDY SCREAMS]

782
01:06:37,254 --> 01:06:39,822
Easy. Easy,
it's all right, Andy. It's all right.

783
01:06:39,865 --> 01:06:43,478
You're not gonna
need this anymore, all right?

784
01:06:43,521 --> 01:06:47,177
But I do. Chucky's in the room,
and he's trying to kill me.

785
01:06:47,221 --> 01:06:49,571
No, Andy.
It's gonna be all right. I'm here now.

786
01:06:49,614 --> 01:06:50,964
And I'm gonna protect you.

787
01:06:51,834 --> 01:06:54,663
Andy. Easy, boy. Easy.

788
01:06:54,706 --> 01:06:56,621
Come on, nobody's here.

789
01:06:56,665 --> 01:06:58,188
No, please.
He'll kill you, too.

790
01:06:58,232 --> 01:06:59,537
Andy, now...

791
01:06:59,581 --> 01:07:02,584
No, please.
Listen to me. Please.

792
01:07:02,627 --> 01:07:05,891
Andy, now this is just gonna sting
you for one second.

793
01:07:07,893 --> 01:07:08,894
[SCREAMS]

794
01:07:16,990 --> 01:07:17,991
[ZAPPING]

795
01:07:20,036 --> 01:07:24,649
Stop! Stop! Stop! Stop!

796
01:07:26,782 --> 01:07:27,783
[LAUGHS]

797
01:07:29,437 --> 01:07:30,525
Stop.

798
01:07:48,108 --> 01:07:49,485
What happened?

799
01:07:49,568 --> 01:07:51,539
Look, miss, could you just excuse us for

800
01:07:51,563 --> 01:07:53,324
- a minute here, all right?
- What?

801
01:07:55,985 --> 01:07:57,421
- What?
- Yeah, yeah.

802
01:07:57,465 --> 01:08:00,335
Fried him to a crisp with the electric shock
machine and then he escaped.

803
01:08:00,381 --> 01:08:01,979
Escaped? Where?

804
01:08:02,052 --> 01:08:05,255
We don't know,
but I bet she does.

805
01:08:10,913 --> 01:08:12,958
Chucky.
You seen Chucky anywhere?

806
01:08:14,003 --> 01:08:16,049
- Who's Chucky?
- Kid's doll.

807
01:08:16,092 --> 01:08:17,583
The same one that was
at the station house.

808
01:08:17,637 --> 01:08:19,226
Have you seen him
anywhere?

809
01:08:19,269 --> 01:08:21,793
What am I gonna know about a doll?
Where are you going?

810
01:08:25,316 --> 01:08:26,511
They think
Andy did it.

811
01:08:26,525 --> 01:08:28,378
I know, the girl said
that Chucky was here,

812
01:08:28,403 --> 01:08:30,019
and that he was
looking for Andy.

813
01:08:30,063 --> 01:08:32,065
- But where would Andy go?
- He'd go home.

814
01:08:32,108 --> 01:08:33,675
I always told him
to go there if he was in trouble.

815
01:08:33,718 --> 01:08:35,633
- Does he have a key?
- It's under the mat.

816
01:08:35,677 --> 01:08:37,462
Come on. Come on.
We don't have much time.

817
01:09:02,965 --> 01:09:04,227
Look, George.

818
01:09:04,271 --> 01:09:06,403
Some child left their doll
in the elevator.

819
01:09:06,436 --> 01:09:07,649
Leave it alone.

820
01:09:07,691 --> 01:09:09,972
Whoever left it there
will come back looking for it.

821
01:09:15,412 --> 01:09:16,805
Ugly doll.

822
01:09:18,807 --> 01:09:20,695
CHUCKY: Fuck you.

823
01:11:03,738 --> 01:11:06,416
[SHOUTS]
Surprise!

824
01:11:08,308 --> 01:11:09,309
[GRUNTS]

825
01:11:37,250 --> 01:11:38,425
Batter up!

826
01:11:38,468 --> 01:11:39,945
[GROANS]

827
01:11:41,254 --> 01:11:42,559
[SIREN BLARING]

828
01:12:01,752 --> 01:12:03,537
[CHANTING IN ANCIENT LANGUAGE]

829
01:12:22,512 --> 01:12:25,167
Give me the power,
I beg of you.

830
01:12:35,960 --> 01:12:38,311
[CONTINUES CHANTING
IN ANCIENT LANGUAGE]

831
01:12:42,880 --> 01:12:44,012
KAREN: Andy!

832
01:12:49,060 --> 01:12:50,323
KAREN: Andy!

833
01:12:50,366 --> 01:12:52,063
MIKE: Andy!
KAREN: Andy!

834
01:12:52,107 --> 01:12:53,804
MIKE: Andy, can you hear me?

835
01:13:00,245 --> 01:13:01,546
KAREN: Andy!

836
01:13:02,509 --> 01:13:03,859
Andy!

837
01:13:08,471 --> 01:13:09,646
[SCREAMING]

838
01:13:11,431 --> 01:13:13,215
KAREN: Andy.

839
01:13:13,258 --> 01:13:15,609
MIKE: Karen, Karen,
are you all right?

840
01:13:15,652 --> 01:13:16,653
[SCREAMS]

841
01:13:19,482 --> 01:13:20,744
Oh, Mike.

842
01:13:20,788 --> 01:13:22,442
Just take care of Andy.

843
01:13:26,707 --> 01:13:28,787
Karen, Karen.

844
01:13:28,813 --> 01:13:30,014
Take this. Take it.

845
01:13:30,058 --> 01:13:31,364
Mike!

846
01:13:31,407 --> 01:13:32,495
[WHIMPERING]

847
01:13:33,670 --> 01:13:34,758
Mommy.

848
01:14:18,715 --> 01:14:20,064
[SCREAMS]

849
01:14:27,768 --> 01:14:28,769
[SCREAMS]

850
01:14:33,730 --> 01:14:35,079
[CLICKING]

851
01:14:35,123 --> 01:14:37,125
CHUCKY: What's wrong?
Gun jammed?

852
01:14:37,168 --> 01:14:38,300
[SCREAMING]

853
01:14:45,786 --> 01:14:47,396
[SCREAMING]

854
01:15:15,729 --> 01:15:16,947
Andy!

855
01:15:16,991 --> 01:15:19,254
Andy, help me.
The matches.

856
01:15:19,863 --> 01:15:21,299
Andy!

857
01:15:21,343 --> 01:15:22,562
Please! Now!

858
01:15:34,748 --> 01:15:37,401
Andy, no, please.

859
01:15:37,838 --> 01:15:40,667
We're friends
to the end. Remember?

860
01:15:40,710 --> 01:15:43,626
This is the end, friend.

861
01:15:45,195 --> 01:15:46,629
[SCREAMING]

862
01:15:53,288 --> 01:15:54,289
[GASPS]

863
01:16:28,453 --> 01:16:29,759
Oh, my baby.

864
01:16:29,803 --> 01:16:32,084
MIKE: Karen? Andy?

865
01:16:32,240 --> 01:16:33,589
You all right?

866
01:16:36,244 --> 01:16:37,854
[GROANING]

867
01:16:41,292 --> 01:16:42,946
Andy, go get me
the first-aid kit

868
01:16:42,990 --> 01:16:44,687
under the kitchen sink
really fast. Okay?

869
01:16:44,731 --> 01:16:46,210
What happened?

870
01:16:46,254 --> 01:16:49,016
Oh, God.
Chucky's dead.

871
01:16:59,789 --> 01:17:01,008
[CRASHING]

872
01:17:01,051 --> 01:17:03,488
Mommy, Chucky's gone.

873
01:17:04,707 --> 01:17:06,317
KAREN: Andy, hurry up.

874
01:17:07,797 --> 01:17:08,968
Andy.

875
01:17:23,160 --> 01:17:24,466
Hello, Andy.

876
01:17:27,295 --> 01:17:28,557
Mommy.

877
01:17:29,689 --> 01:17:31,677
Mommy.

878
01:17:32,605 --> 01:17:34,316
Mommy!

879
01:17:34,432 --> 01:17:35,520
[SCREAMS]

880
01:17:37,827 --> 01:17:40,163
Give me the boy,
and I'll let you live.

881
01:17:40,227 --> 01:17:42,997
Do you hear me?
Give me the boy.

882
01:17:57,978 --> 01:17:59,414
[KAREN SCREAMING]

883
01:18:06,029 --> 01:18:07,601
Mommy!

884
01:18:12,296 --> 01:18:13,820
[SCREAMING]

885
01:18:18,868 --> 01:18:20,609
[CRYING]

886
01:18:40,020 --> 01:18:41,978
CHUCKY: Give me the boy.

887
01:19:10,920 --> 01:19:12,095
[GASPS]

888
01:19:44,693 --> 01:19:45,694
[CLICKING]

889
01:19:51,831 --> 01:19:53,049
JOHN: What the hell's
going on here?

890
01:19:53,093 --> 01:19:55,573
Oh, hey, hey, hey.

891
01:19:55,617 --> 01:19:56,705
MIKE: Karen.

892
01:20:03,973 --> 01:20:05,453
Oh, Jesus.

893
01:20:09,762 --> 01:20:11,633
JOHN: Yeah, I got a cop down here.
Multiple stab wounds.

894
01:20:11,676 --> 01:20:15,506
The Brewster Apartments
on North Grand Street. Make it fast.

895
01:20:15,550 --> 01:20:17,813
All right, they're gonna be here in 10 minutes.
Now, tell me what happened.

896
01:20:17,857 --> 01:20:20,729
The kid was right.
The doll's alive.

897
01:20:20,773 --> 01:20:22,339
He almost got
the three of us.

898
01:20:22,383 --> 01:20:25,342
Come on,
what are you talking about?

899
01:20:25,386 --> 01:20:28,432
You don't believe me? All right, well, go on.
Check it out in the hall.

900
01:20:28,476 --> 01:20:30,086
It's scattered
all over the place.

901
01:20:30,130 --> 01:20:32,750
But don't touch it.
Do you understand me?

902
01:20:32,784 --> 01:20:34,395
Don't you touch
one part of it!

903
01:20:34,438 --> 01:20:36,049
All right, look.
Take it easy, okay?

904
01:20:36,092 --> 01:20:38,573
Just relax yourself,
all right? All right.

905
01:21:17,351 --> 01:21:20,021
Okay, Mike. I'd like you to take a look
at this thing, okay?

906
01:21:20,074 --> 01:21:22,051
Because there's no way
this thing's alive.

907
01:21:23,792 --> 01:21:25,402
I thought I told you
not to touch it.

908
01:21:25,446 --> 01:21:27,013
Mike, will you be
sensible?

909
01:21:27,056 --> 01:21:29,479
Come on, look.
It's as dead as they come. It's dead.

910
01:21:30,059 --> 01:21:31,234
[SCREAMS]

911
01:21:31,278 --> 01:21:33,436
CHUCKY: Choke him!
Kill him!

912
01:21:33,480 --> 01:21:36,022
I'll rip his throat out.

913
01:21:36,065 --> 01:21:37,276
Kill him!

914
01:21:40,591 --> 01:21:41,679
Kill him.

915
01:21:45,945 --> 01:21:51,898
Kill him now! Strangle him!
Don't let go!

916
01:21:56,085 --> 01:21:57,217
JOHN: God.

917
01:22:06,008 --> 01:22:09,011
Kill them! Kill them!
Kill them all!

918
01:22:09,055 --> 01:22:10,839
The heart.
Shoot him in the heart.

919
01:22:14,538 --> 01:22:17,714
[SCREAMS]

920
01:22:36,734 --> 01:22:39,128
Hi, I'm Chucky.

921
01:22:39,172 --> 01:22:43,661
Wanna play?

922
01:22:53,142 --> 01:22:54,970
You believe me now?

923
01:22:55,014 --> 01:22:56,328
Yeah.

924
01:22:58,452 --> 01:23:00,584
But who's gonna believe me?

925
01:23:01,716 --> 01:23:02,804
[SIREN BLARING]

926
01:23:05,720 --> 01:23:06,764
Come on.

927
01:23:09,028 --> 01:23:11,117
All right. Ready?
Here we go.

928
01:23:17,210 --> 01:23:18,298
Come on.

929
01:23:31,572 --> 01:23:33,052
Andy.

930
01:23:33,095 --> 01:23:36,272
Come on. We're gonna go to
the hospital with Mike.

931
01:23:36,316 --> 01:23:37,621
Let's go.

